/* Copyright 2026 Rhett Creighton - Apache License 2.0
 *
 * WINDOWS X86-64 EXACT MODULE CAPABILITY OVERRIDES.
 *
 * config/module_capabilities.def remains the portable/Linux snapshot and the
 * cross-target package-claim base. A source path can select materially
 * different external entry points under _WIN32: a refusal stub may reach
 * nothing while a native arm reaches Win32 APIs absent from ELF. One union
 * row cannot stay symmetric against both object graphs.
 *
 * Each row here REPLACES the portable row while the closure gate grades a
 * native Windows epoch. CAP_NONE is an explicit empty override, not a
 * capability class. Package capability derivation unions this supplement
 * with the portable table so a package declares everything reachable on any
 * supported target.
 *
 * Generated as a reviewed snapshot on 2026-08-30 from the complete native
 * MinGW C23 epoch:
 *   build/dev-obj/epochs/e352e6957ebde912f5961fb012d612872b28b877aa890300f7bcf805b33013dc
 *   2060 translation-unit objects after excluding the generated
 *   restart-base.o aggregate.
 * Ordering is alphabetical by source path and carries no meaning. */

